                EVENT - set_npc_standing_text - scribe_halden ("I record what happened... and what didn't. Both are equally true."):
                EVENT - set_npc_standing_text - vex ("Every possibility cancels another. The tighter the contradiction, the easier it is to slip through."):
                EVENT - show_npc - mira (region_city_shopweapons):
                EVENT - set_npc_standing_text - mira ("Fancy meeting you here, I see you found the Bracelet of Existence."):
            ► COMPLETED:
                Scribe Halden - You were never here. And yet... here you are. I recorded your arrival yesterday. And tomorrow.:
                Kaera - How can both be true?:
                Halden - That is the question that keeps me here. The only clue I have left is this old legend.:
                Halden - It speaks of a box that opens only when two impossible things are true at once.:
                Chock - (frustrated) So we're chasing fairy tales now?:
                Moxie - No, this is perfect. A box that only works when it shouldn't. I *love* this place.:
                Kade - If both versions of events are true, then logic itself is broken. We're not solving a puzzle. We're exploiting the break.:
                Halden - Take the legend to Vex. Maybe she can make two impossible things exist at the same time. I never could.:
                EVENT - set_npc_standing_text - scribe_halden ("Compliance is mandatory. Non-compliance is impossible. You are already in violation."):
                EVENT - award_item - puzzle_box_legend:
                EVENT - award_task - Deliver Puzzle Box Legend To Vex

